{"id": "newfields-Q4791095", "status": "ok", "meta": "Aristotle as a ragged beggar-philosopher with a deeply creased face, painted by Jusepe de Ribera in 1637 for the Prince of Liechtenstein.", "about": "Aristotle appears as a ragged beggar-philosopher, a popular idea in the seventeenth century, with deep creases in his face and hands. Jusepe de Ribera painted him in 1637 as one of six portraits of ancient philosophers ordered by the Prince of Liechtenstein. Light falls on him in a way that recalls Caravaggio. Ribera signed the painting across the papers in Aristotle's hand, and he added español to his name to stress where he came from.", "museum_record": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File%3ARibera%2C_Jusepe_de_-_Aristotle_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg", "inventory_number": "", "dimensions": "", "credit_line": "", "sources": ["https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File%3ARibera%2C_Jusepe_de_-_Aristotle_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg", "https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q4791095", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aristotle_(Ribera)"], "check": "clean"}
